Attribution
-----------

The rules, the binding parameter table and the four artifact schemas implemented
here are defined by the project booklet "משחק שוטרים וגנבים P2P בין סוכני AI"
v3.0.0 by Dr. Yoram Segal, University of Haifa. The booklet and the accompanying
software guidelines are the lecturer's copyrighted work and are not distributed
with this repository.

The reference simulator at https://github.com/rmisegal/Game-P2P-Cop-Chase was
read for its four JSON artifact schemas. No code from it was copied; the booklet
states that where the code and the booklet disagree, the booklet governs, and
this implementation follows the booklet.

Third-party libraries, each under its own license:
  fastmcp            Apache-2.0    peer-to-peer MCP transport
  httpx              BSD-3-Clause  HTTP client used by the Ollama provider
  psutil             BSD-3-Clause  hardware collection for the Step-0 declaration
  google-api-python-client, google-auth, google-auth-oauthlib
                     Apache-2.0    send-only Gmail reporting
  anthropic          MIT           optional trash-talk provider
  matplotlib, numpy  PSF / BSD     analysis notebook figures
  pytest, ruff       MIT           test and lint tooling
